# che-android-studio VM options for Android Studio / ASfP, supplied to the IDE
# via the STUDIO_VM_OPTIONS env var (the entrypoint points it here). Kept
# separate from ASfP's bundled bin/studio64.vmoptions so an IDE upgrade can't
# clobber it and we don't have to edit a vendored file.
#
# UI scaling is not set here because it is not KNOWABLE here: the right value is
# the CLIENT's devicePixelRatio, which only the browser can report (see
# kasmvnc-subpath-fix.html). The workspace supplies it at launch as
# -Dsun.java2d.uiScale via _JAVA_OPTIONS.
#
# CORRECTING AN EARLIER NOTE. This file used to say -Dsun.java2d.uiScale
# "rendered poorly (chrome scaled but editor font did not)". That does not
# reproduce. Screenshotting the running IDE at each setting showed the opposite
# split: Settings > Appearance > Zoom (NotRoamableUiSettings/ideScale) at 200%
# scaled the FONTS ONLY, leaving the toolbar, icons, tree rows, dialogs and
# status bar small — while -Dsun.java2d.uiScale=2 scaled chrome, icons, tree,
# editor and console together. sun.java2d.uiScale is the setting to use; ideScale
# is a personal zoom to sit on top of it, and the two compound, so a session
# that sets the JVM scale pins Zoom back to 100%.

# Custom window decorations: let the IDE draw its own header/title bar (paired
# with openbox <decor>no</decor>) for a clean kiosk frame.
-Dide.win.frame.decorations=true
